# The region set this deployment actually builds. Read by scripts/graphhopper.sh
# under GH_REGION_SET=custom; one "geofabrik/path|minlon,minlat,maxlon,maxlat"
# per line, an empty bbox meaning take the whole extract, '#' comments stripped.
#
# ⚠ THE FIRST THREE DATA LINES ARE REQUIRED. `regions_for_set()` is a plain case
# statement: `custom` REPLACES the set, it does not extend `demo`. A file
# missing the Sri Lanka, Greater London or Noord-Holland lines takes out the
# TEST_LOCATIONS, verify_selfhosted.py's oldest assertions, and the London
# origin the layout gate drives the app from.
#
# ⚠ ONE CITY, SEVERAL LINES is deliberate, not duplication. A bounding box does
# not stop at an administrative boundary, and a cut can only contain what its
# extract holds — so a box that crosses one is listed once per extract it
# touches, same box each time, and `osmium merge` deduplicates the ways that
# appear in both. Dropping the "redundant" New Jersey line does not make the
# build smaller; it makes Newark silently absent from a graph that still
# claims Manhattan's box.
#
# The shape of this file is the shape of what a 12 GB VM can serve. Whole
# countries at US or European scale cannot fit — Geofabrik lists
# north-america/us at 11.3 GB and europe at 32.5 GB of extract before any
# graph is built from either, and this file's 6.3 GB of merged input already
# produced a 13 GB graph that took three and a half hours to import — so
# coverage is Sri Lanka entire plus a box around every metro worth walking in
# that the graph can afford, roughly a degree on a side, drawn around where
# people actually are. The measured costs, and the ceiling they ran into, are
# in PROGRESS.md §19; the serve-side arithmetic is in scripts/graphhopper.sh
# next to GH_DATAACCESS.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sri Lanka — the whole country, and the start of the expansion order.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Sri Lanka entire. The demo set cut this to a 1x1 degree box around Colombo,
# which put Ella (6.875 N, 81.038 E) 76 km outside the eastern edge and told a
# Sri Lankan user that Meander does not cover their country. 143.7 MB of
# extract against the 45.7 MB cut brings in Kandy, Galle, Nuwara Eliya, Jaffna
# and Trincomalee as well, and Ella at 1,041 m is the first test location that
# is not at sea level.
asia/sri-lanka|

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The two original European boxes, made honest and then filled.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Unchanged from the demo set: ±0.5° around the Hyde Park / Euston Road
# cluster. The greater-london extract stops at the Greater London boundary,
# which is well inside this box — the england line beneath it is what fills
# Watford, Luton, St Albans and Windsor, so the box finally contains what it
# always claimed. (The manifest used to claim the full box on this line alone;
# clip_to_extract in graphhopper.sh now prevents exactly that.)
europe/united-kingdom/england/greater-london|-0.65,51.02,0.36,52.03
europe/united-kingdom/england|-0.65,51.02,0.36,52.03

# The Vondelpark box, unchanged — and the two lines that fill its southern
# half. The box has always spanned 51.86–52.86, and the noord-holland extract
# ends near 52.16, so Rotterdam, Den Haag, Leiden and Utrecht were inside the
# claimed box and absent from the graph. The zuid-holland box is wider than
# the original on its west edge for a reason: Den Haag's centre is at 4.30 E
# and the inherited 4.36 E edge missed the seat of government by six
# hundredths of a degree. Utrecht's runs to 5.65 E so Amersfoort comes with it.
europe/netherlands/noord-holland|4.36,51.86,5.37,52.86
europe/netherlands/zuid-holland|4.0,51.75,5.37,52.4
europe/netherlands/utrecht|4.9,51.9,5.65,52.3

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# United States — second in the expansion order. Metro boxes, not states:
# the places, not the interstate between them.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# New York. The box crosses the Hudson and the state line with it — New Jersey
# holds Newark, Jersey City and Hoboken, and the north-east corner is
# Connecticut's Stamford. Three extracts, one box.
north-america/us/new-york|-74.6,40.2,-73.3,41.2
north-america/us/new-jersey|-74.6,40.2,-73.3,41.2
north-america/us/connecticut|-74.6,40.2,-73.3,41.2

# Southern California as one box rather than Los Angeles and San Diego as two.
# Two adjacent boxes left Oceanside in the gap between them; one box holds the
# whole LA–Orange–Inland Empire–San Diego corridor with no seam to fall into.
north-america/us/california/socal|-118.95,32.55,-116.9,34.45

# The Bay Area: San Francisco, Oakland, Berkeley, San Jose.
north-america/us/california/norcal|-122.75,37.2,-121.7,38.05

# Chicago, whose lakefront crosses into Indiana at Hammond and Gary.
north-america/us/illinois|-88.35,41.45,-87.2,42.15
north-america/us/indiana|-88.35,41.45,-87.2,42.15

# Boston to the New Hampshire line, with the sliver of Rhode Island the box's
# south-west corner clips. Providence gets its own box below.
north-america/us/massachusetts|-71.55,41.95,-70.6,42.7
north-america/us/rhode-island|-71.55,41.95,-70.6,42.7
north-america/us/rhode-island|-71.55,41.65,-71.2,41.95

# Washington and Baltimore share one tall box: DC itself, all of suburban
# Maryland and Annapolis, and Arlington, Alexandria and the Dulles corridor
# on the Virginia side.
north-america/us/district-of-columbia|-77.55,38.55,-76.35,39.45
north-america/us/maryland|-77.55,38.55,-76.35,39.45
north-america/us/virginia|-77.55,38.55,-76.35,39.45

# Philadelphia — with Camden and Trenton across the Delaware, and Wilmington
# at the box's south-west.
north-america/us/pennsylvania|-75.6,39.6,-74.7,40.4
north-america/us/new-jersey|-75.6,39.6,-74.7,40.4
north-america/us/delaware|-75.6,39.6,-74.7,40.4

# Seattle, Tacoma to Everett.
north-america/us/washington|-122.55,47.15,-121.9,48.05

# Portland, whose twin Vancouver is across the Columbia in Washington.
north-america/us/oregon|-123.1,45.2,-122.2,45.9
north-america/us/washington|-123.1,45.2,-122.2,45.9

# Florida: the Miami–Fort Lauderdale–West Palm strip, and Orlando with the
# theme parks at its south-west.
north-america/us/florida|-80.55,25.4,-79.95,26.75
north-america/us/florida|-81.75,28.2,-81.1,28.85

# Texas, four times from one extract: Houston out to Galveston, Dallas–Fort
# Worth, Austin, San Antonio.
north-america/us/texas|-95.85,29.2,-94.7,30.15
north-america/us/texas|-97.6,32.5,-96.45,33.15
north-america/us/texas|-98.05,30.05,-97.45,30.65
north-america/us/texas|-98.75,29.2,-98.2,29.75

# Phoenix–Scottsdale–Mesa.
north-america/us/arizona|-112.55,33.15,-111.55,33.85

# Atlanta.
north-america/us/georgia|-84.75,33.45,-84.05,34.05

# Denver and Boulder.
north-america/us/colorado|-105.35,39.45,-104.6,40.1

# Minneapolis–St Paul.
north-america/us/minnesota|-93.6,44.6,-92.85,45.25

# Las Vegas, west far enough to take in the Red Rock scenic loop.
north-america/us/nevada|-115.5,35.9,-114.85,36.35

# New Orleans.
north-america/us/louisiana|-90.3,29.75,-89.85,30.2

# Honolulu — in practice all of O'ahu, which is smaller than most of the
# boxes on this list.
north-america/us/hawaii|-158.3,21.25,-157.6,21.75

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Europe — third in the expansion order.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Paris, Versailles, Saint-Denis, down to Fontainebleau.
europe/france/ile-de-france|1.9,48.35,2.9,49.15

# The Côte d'Azur from Cannes to Menton. Monaco is a hole in every French
# extract — it is its own country and its own (1 MB) extract — so the second
# line is what stops the principality being a blank spot ringed by coverage.
# The third is the ridge above Menton, which is Italy: nord-ovest is already
# paid for at Milan, and the alternative is a border sliver inside the box
# that no extract filled.
europe/france/provence-alpes-cote-d-azur|6.95,43.5,7.55,43.85
europe/monaco|6.95,43.5,7.55,43.85
europe/italy/nord-ovest|6.95,43.5,7.55,43.85

# Marseille and Aix-en-Provence, from the same PACA extract.
europe/france/provence-alpes-cote-d-azur|5.2,43.15,5.65,43.55

# Berlin, whose ring ends in Brandenburg — Potsdam is the second line.
europe/germany/berlin|12.9,52.25,13.85,52.75
europe/germany/brandenburg|12.9,52.25,13.85,52.75

# Munich.
europe/germany/bayern/oberbayern|11.2,47.9,11.95,48.45

# Hamburg is a city-state: Norderstedt is Schleswig-Holstein and everything
# south of the Elbe is Niedersachsen, so one box needs three extracts.
europe/germany/hamburg|9.7,53.35,10.35,53.75
europe/germany/schleswig-holstein|9.7,53.35,10.35,53.75
europe/germany/niedersachsen|9.7,53.35,10.35,53.75

# Frankfurt, Darmstadt, Hanau. The west edge stops at 8.45 E because the far
# bank of the Rhein is Rheinland-Pfalz — Mainz and Wiesbaden wait for a round
# that imports it.
europe/germany/hessen|8.45,49.8,8.95,50.3

# Cologne, Bonn and Düsseldorf: one Rhein corridor, two Regierungsbezirke.
europe/germany/nordrhein-westfalen/koeln-regbez|6.6,50.6,7.25,51.35
europe/germany/nordrhein-westfalen/duesseldorf-regbez|6.6,50.6,7.25,51.35

# Brussels, Antwerp, Ghent and Bruges — and the strip of Zeeuws-Vlaanderen
# along the box's north edge, which is the Netherlands even though everything
# around it on three sides is Belgium.
europe/belgium|3.1,50.7,4.6,51.35
europe/netherlands/zeeland|3.1,50.7,4.6,51.35

# Madrid, out to El Escorial.
europe/spain|-4.2,40.05,-3.3,40.75

# Barcelona, with Sitges and Montserrat.
europe/spain|1.75,41.2,2.55,41.75

# Valencia.
europe/spain|-0.65,39.25,-0.15,39.75

# Seville.
europe/spain|-6.15,37.2,-5.7,37.6

# Rome, from Ostia to Tivoli.
europe/italy/centro|12.15,41.6,12.95,42.15

# Florence, Pisa and Lucca in one Tuscan box.
europe/italy/centro|10.25,43.5,11.55,44.05

# Milan up to Como — where the last kilometre before the lake's border towns
# is Switzerland, hence the second line from an extract this file already
# pays for at Zurich.
europe/italy/nord-ovest|8.85,45.25,9.55,45.85
europe/switzerland|8.85,45.25,9.55,45.85

# Venice and Padua.
europe/italy/nord-est|11.8,45.2,12.7,45.75

# Naples, Pompeii, Sorrento and the Amalfi coast.
europe/italy/sud|14.05,40.5,14.7,41.0

# Lisbon, Sintra and Cascais.
europe/portugal|-9.55,38.5,-8.9,39.0

# Porto.
europe/portugal|-8.75,40.95,-8.35,41.35

# Vienna.
europe/austria|16.05,47.95,16.75,48.4

# Zurich, Zug and Lucerne.
europe/switzerland|8.15,46.95,8.9,47.55

# Prague.
europe/czech-republic|14.15,49.85,14.8,50.3

# Warsaw.
europe/poland/mazowieckie|20.65,52.0,21.35,52.45

# Krakow and Wieliczka.
europe/poland/malopolskie|19.65,49.9,20.3,50.25

# Budapest.
europe/hungary|18.8,47.3,19.4,47.75

# Copenhagen and Malmö–Lund: one urban area, one bridge, two countries.
europe/denmark|12.3,55.5,13.25,55.95
europe/sweden|12.3,55.5,13.25,55.95

# Stockholm.
europe/sweden|17.7,59.15,18.4,59.55

# Oslo. The box stops at 59.999 N and that is not a joke: SRTM elevation ends
# at 60 N, the *_elevation custom models and the incline constraint read
# elevation, and a graph whose Nordmarka trails all report 0 m of climb would
# be the accessible preset lying about hills. Helsinki and Reykjavik are not
# in this file for the same reason.
europe/norway|10.5,59.75,11.0,59.999

# Athens and Piraeus.
europe/greece|23.5,37.85,24.05,38.2

# Dublin.
europe/ireland-and-northern-ireland|-6.6,53.15,-6.0,53.65

# Edinburgh and Glasgow in one central-belt box — Edinburgh being the
# verify_selfhosted.py location that has been skipped since the script was
# written. The england line is the Cheviot corner of the box.
europe/united-kingdom/scotland|-4.55,55.6,-2.85,56.1
europe/united-kingdom/england|-4.55,55.6,-2.85,56.1

# Manchester and Liverpool, with the Deeside corner of the box that is Wales.
europe/united-kingdom/england|-3.1,53.2,-1.95,53.75
europe/united-kingdom/wales|-3.1,53.2,-1.95,53.75

# Birmingham and Coventry.
europe/united-kingdom/england|-2.25,52.3,-1.45,52.7
